+<entry>
+<title>RUSTSEC-2026-0593: Vulnerability in pqcrypto-dilithium</title>
+<id>https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0593.html</id>
+<updated>2026-11-22T12:00:00+00:00</updated>
+<category term="crypto-failure"/>
+<link href="https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0593.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="RUSTSEC-2026-0593: Vulnerability in pqcrypto-dilithium"/>
+<published>2026-11-22T12:00:00+00:00</published>
+<summary xml:lang="en">Dilithium verification accepts non-conforming signatures with the `avx2` feature</summary>
+<content xml:lang="en" type="html">
+<article>
+<span class="floating-menu">
+<a href="https://github.com/RustSec/advisory-db/commits/main/crates/pqcrypto-dilithium/RUSTSEC-2026-0593.md">History</a> ⋅
+<a href="https://github.com/RustSec/advisory-db/edit/main/crates/pqcrypto-dilithium/RUSTSEC-2026-0593.md">Edit</a> ⋅
+<a href="https://api.osv.dev/v1/vulns/RUSTSEC-2026-0593">JSON (OSV)</a>
+</span>
+<header>
+<h1>
+RUSTSEC-2026-0593
+</h1>
+<span class="subtitle">
+<p>Dilithium verification accepts non-conforming signatures with the <code>avx2</code> feature</p>
+</span>
+</header>
+<dl>
+<dt id="reported">Reported</dt>
+<dd>
+<time datetime="2026-11-21">
+November 21, 2026
+</time>
+</dd>
+<dt id="issued">Issued</dt>
+<dd>
+<time datetime="2026-11-22">
+November 22, 2026
+</time>
+</dd>
+<dt id="package">Package</dt>
+<dd>
+<a href="/packages/pqcrypto-dilithium.html">pqcrypto-dilithium</a>
+(<a href="https://crates.io/crates/pqcrypto-dilithium">crates.io</a>)
+</dd>
+<dt id="type">Type</dt>
+<dd>
+Vulnerability
+</dd>
+<dt id="categories">Categories</dt>
+<dd>
+<ul>
+<li>
+<a href="/categories/crypto-failure.html">crypto-failure</a>
+</li>
+</ul>
+</dd>
+<dt id="keywords">Keywords</dt>
+<dd>
+<a href="/keywords/dilithium.html">#dilithium</a>
+<a href="/keywords/signature.html">#signature</a>
+<a href="/keywords/verification.html">#verification</a>
+<a href="/keywords/avx2.html">#avx2</a>
+</dd>
+<dt id="details">References</dt>
+<dd>
+<ul>
+<li>
+<a href="https://github.com/RatioLabsEU/pqc-field-notes/tree/main/advisories/2026-mldsa-avx2-verifier">
+https://github.com/RatioLabsEU/pqc-field-notes/tree/main/advisories/2026-mldsa-avx2-verifier
+</a>
+</li>
+<li>
+<a href="https://github.com/pq-crystals/dilithium/issues/113">
+https://github.com/pq-crystals/dilithium/issues/113
+</a>
+</li>
+<li>
+<a href="https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0586.html">
+https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0586.html
+</a>
+</li>
+</ul>
+</dd>
+<dt id="patched">Patched</dt>
+<dd>
+no patched versions
+</dd>
+<dt>Affected Architectures</dt>
+<dd>
+<ul>
+<li>
+<code>x86_64</code>
+</li>
+</ul>
+</dd>
+</dl>
+<h3 id="description">Description</h3>
+<p>With the default <code>avx2</code> feature on x86_64 and a CPU that supports AVX2,
+<code>pqcrypto-dilithium</code> verifies signatures with PQClean's AVX2 implementation of
+Dilithium. That implementation predates two upstream fixes
+(<a href="https://github.com/pq-crystals/dilithium/issues/113">pq-crystals/dilithium#113</a>,
+3 June 2026), the same ones described in RUSTSEC-2026-0586 for <code>pqcrypto-mldsa</code>:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>the verifier does not check that the infinity norm of <code>z</code> is below
+<code>γ1 − β</code>, so it accepts signatures that the crate's own portable
+implementation rejects;</li>
+<li>
+<code>use_hint_avx()</code> mishandles a boundary case, so one class of valid
+signatures is rejected.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>Creating an accepted out-of-bound signature requires the private key. The
+practical effect is that verification results differ between this crate with
+AVX2 and the same crate without it.</p>
+<p>Tested on version 0.5.0: for each of dilithium2, dilithium3 and dilithium5, 20
+signatures with <code>z</code> out of bound are accepted with AVX2 and rejected by the
+portable code, and 2 valid signatures that exercise the <code>use_hint</code> boundary
+are rejected with AVX2 and accepted by the portable code. This crate
+implements a pre-standard version of the scheme, so the Wycheproof ML-DSA
+vectors do not apply; the test signatures are built with the crate's own
+signer.</p>
+<p>The crate is unmaintained (see RUSTSEC-2024-0380) and no patched version is
+expected. Disabling the <code>avx2</code> feature avoids the affected code.</p>
+<p id="license" class="license">Advisory available under <a href="https://spdx.org/licenses/CC0-1.0.html">CC0-1.0</a>
+license.
+</p>
+</article>
+</content>
+</entry>
